Changelog: 11-10-2026 17:23:05

The header shows whether GitHub built the last push (GitHub: building, passed or failed): the workflow runs of its
commit, from the public Actions API with an ETag, every 30 s while a build runs and every 5 minutes otherwise, and at
Refresh. Hover lists each run; a click opens the failed or running run. A run seen running that finishes gives a
desktop notification (notify-send) and flags the window.

Changelog: 11-10-2026 17:04:46

Run from checkout has a Manual (local) icon after the apps: it serves the manual from the checkout with mkdocs serve
(on 127.0.0.1:8765, the path of site_url) and opens it in the browser once the server answers. When it already runs,
a click only opens the page again. The manual's release front end section says so.

Changelog: 11-10-2026 14:34:03

New page, Run from checkout: every app window in the checkout as an icon (each package with a __main__.py under
apps/, tests and the checkout-only apps left out), with its name, version and icon. A click starts that app from the
checkout, to try a change before its release: python -m <package> with this venv and the checkout's core on the path,
as run.sh starts this app (plan.launch_targets and plan.launch_command). Apps that portal/apps.toml marks
changes_board ask first. Each app runs in its own session, so it keeps running when the window closes, and writes its
output to ~/.cache/bc250-release/run/<package>.log; when it stops with an error, the end of that log shows on the
page. docs/portal.md describes the page. Tests: the targets and their command, the page (start, the question for board
apps, the log tail of a failed app) and a real start that keeps its output in the log.

Changelog: 11-10-2026 12:34:52

The board test buttons of step 2 are renamed: Check updates is now Test updates, Check release is now Test release, in the window, its hint, the command list and docs/portal.md. They do what they did.

Changelog: 11-10-2026 12:19:03

A Refresh button in the header reads the checkout and its tags again, for changes made in a terminal while the window is open (commits, reverts, tags, edited files). It keeps what was entered: the ticks, versions and notes of step 1, and the portal version and notes of step 2. A version is kept only when it was typed or picked, not when it is still the one offered, so a version changed in a terminal shows its new choices.

Changelog: 11-10-2026 09:24:18

BC250 Suite Releases becomes an app of its own, moved from tools/: the window (tools/release_ui.py, now bc250_suite_releases/main_window.py), the release logic (tools/release_plan.py, now plan.py), the board checks (tools/check-release.sh, now check-release.sh), its icon and its tests. It keeps the name, the app id bc250-release and its settings. run.sh starts it with the checkout's dev venv (--list prints the overview with the system python3); install.sh makes the launcher, menu entry and Desktop icon for this checkout. It has a .standalone marker (not in the portal) and a .checkout-only marker: it edits the checkout it lives in, so it has no releases, the release tool leaves it out and build_release.py refuses its tags. The footer shows its version and the checkout it edits.
